The grid is a list of 3, 0, 8, 4, 2, 4, 5, 7, 9, 2, 6, 3, 0, 3, 1, and 0.
The size is 4.
The rowtops is a list of 4 zeros.
The columntops is a list of 4 zeros.
For every row from 0 to size minus 1.
For every column from 0 to size minus 1.
The value is item (row times size plus column) of grid.
If value is more than item row of rowtops, set item row of rowtops to value.
If value is more than item column of columntops, set item column of columntops to value.

The total is 0.
For every row from 0 to size minus 1.
For every column from 0 to size minus 1.
The spot is row times size plus column.
The value is item spot of grid.
The ceiling is item row of rowtops.
If item column of columntops is less than ceiling, set ceiling to item column of columntops.
Add ceiling minus value to total.

Show total.
